title: 'fix(asset-conversion): use full balances for pool prices'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: "# Description\n\nFixes asset-conversion pool price and liquidity calculations\
    \ to use the full pool balances instead of reducible balances.\n\nThe previous\
    \ logic could calculate reserves from reducible balances, which can exclude protected\
    \ funds and understate the amount held by the pool account. This PR routes the\
    \ relevant calculations through the pallet reserve helper and updates the shared\
    \ balance helper to return the full asset balance.\n\nAn example of a problem\
    \ is found on Polkadot Asset Hub (address `163CRvzDQ8JHZfmufa86zA7BfDY7NToUSqmWbpDq5kwDYSmH`,\
    \ DOT <> USDC pool). Someone transferred a WUD to the account, and now the reducible\
    \ balance substracts the ED, giving a wrong quote.\n\n## Integration\n\nDownstream\
    \ runtimes using `pallet-asset-conversion` should receive this as a patch-level\
    \ bug fix. No migration or configuration change is required.\n\n## Review Notes\n\
    \nThe change affects reserve reads used by:\n\n* liquidity deposit calculations\n\
    * liquidity withdrawal calculations\n* buy/sell price estimations\n\nThe modified\
    \ paths now use the same reserve source as swap execution. `get_balance` now returns\
    \ `T::Assets::balance(...)` so callers that need the owner\u2019s total balance\
    \ do not receive reducible-balance semantics.\n\n# Checklist\n\n* [x] My PR includes\
    \ a detailed description as outlined in the \"Description\" and its two subsections\
    \ above.\n* [x] My PR follows the labeling requirements of this project (at minimum\
    \ one label for `T` required)\n* [x] I have made corresponding changes to the\
    \ documentation (if applicable)\n* [x] I have added tests that prove my fix is\
    \ effective or that my feature works (if applicable)"
crates:
- name: pallet-asset-conversion
  bump: patch
